'''Rune Haako''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[Neimoidian]] official who was a [[Settlement Officer]] of the [[Trade Federation]] and closely worked with [[Viceroy of the Trade Federation|Viceroy]] [[Nute Gunray]] as his [[lieutenant]] during the [[Invasion of Naboo]]. Haako continued to serve the Trade Federation as a high ranking member of the [[Executive Separatist Council|Separatist Council]] throughout the [[Clone Wars]] until his [[death]] at the [[Mission to Mustafar|end]] of the war.

==Biography==
===Invasion of Naboo===
{{Quote|Captain, we've searched the ship and there is no trace of the Jedi. They may have gotten on one of your landing craft.''"<br />"''If they're down here, sir, we'll find them.|Rune Haako and OOM-9|<ref name="Episode I" />}}
[[File:HaakoGunrayPalpy-Ep1.png|thumb|left|250px|Rune Haako with Nute Gunray and Darth Sidious's hologram on Naboo in the Theed Royal Palace.]]
[[Reproduction|Born]] on [[Neimoidia]]<ref name="Geektionary" /> some point before [[32 BBY]], Rune Haako was [[Viceroy of the Trade Federation|Viceroy]] [[Nute Gunray]]'s right hand [[Gender|man]], [[Settlement Officer]] and [[Lieutenant]] during the [[Invasion of Naboo]]. He, Gunray, and [[Daultay Dofine|Dofine]] schemed with [[Sith Lord]] [[Darth Sidious]] in order to achieve greater profits. On Sidious's orders, they made a [[blockade]] on [[Naboo]], because of the new taxation of the formerly [[Free Trade Zone]]s, and later invaded the [[planet]]. The [[Neimoidian]]s attempted to make [[Queen]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] sign a treaty to make the invasion legal by threatening to starve the [[Naboo (people)|people]] of the planet, but she successfully escaped the planet.<ref name="Episode I" />

To ensure all went according to his plan, Sidious sent his [[Sith apprentice|apprentice]] Darth Maul to oversee the occupation and to keep an [[eye]] on the [[Trade Federation]] leadership, which greatly unnerved the naturally cowardly Neimoidians. Gunray held [[Governor]] [[Sio Bibble]] [[prisoner]] and [[OOM-9]] informed Gunray that they would soon draw out the [[Gungan]]s and [[Death|kill]] them. Gunray, Haako and Maul assured Sidious that the Federation will win and that Amidala would soon be forced to return in order to save her people. As they predicted, Amidala [[Battle of Naboo|returned]]. Dofine perished and Gunray and Haako were sent to [[Coruscant]],<ref name="Episode I" /> but ultimately they remained free.<ref name="Episode II" />

===Clone Wars===
[[File:Haako_on_Geonosis.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Viceroy Gunray, Settlement Officer Haako, and Count Dooku on Geonosis.]]
During the [[Separatist Crisis]], Gunray, Haako and their partners from planets and corporations were invited to [[Geonosis]] by [[Count]] [[Dooku]], Sidious's new apprentice. Gunray and Haako [[Geonosian accord|pledged]] the Trade Federation's support to the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] and asked that in return Dooku kill the now Senator Amidala, the Federation's most hated enemy, for revenge. Gunray, Haako, Dooku, and [[Archduke]] [[Poggle the Lesser]] oversaw the failed execution of [[Jedi Knight]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], his [[Padawan]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] and Amidala in the [[Petranaki Arena]], who were saved by the [[Jedi]] and the new [[Grand Army of the Republic]]. Traveling to the [[Geonosian War Room|Geonosian Command Center]], the two Neimoidians joined the other [[Executive Separatist Council|Separatist Council]] members and saw with their own eyes the [[First Battle of Geonosis]] via [[hologram]]. Haako declared it vital that the Federation [[starship]]s be launched into space before retreating in a [[Sheathipede-class transport shuttle|''Sheathipede''-class shuttle]].<ref name="Episode II" />

===Death===
{{Quote|Stop! No!|Haako's last words|<ref name="Episode III" />}}
[[File:Haako_pray_for_mercy_from_vader.jpg|left|thumb|250px|Haako begs for mercy from Darth Vader, moments before his death.]]
At the end of the war, the Separatist Council was called by [[General]] [[Grievous]] to [[Utapau]], following the [[Battle of Coruscant|death]] of Dooku, and were sent to [[Mustafar]] where they resided up until the end of the war. Promised a great reward by Lord Sidious, Haako and the others waited for it to arrive, unaware that they were in fact to be [[Mission to Mustafar|killed]] by his new apprentice [[Darth]] Vader, on Sidious's orders.<ref name="Episode III" />

When Vader arrived, he proceeded to cut down all in his path. At one point, Haako pleaded with the Sith Lord to cease the massacre, to no avail, and retreated into the conference room with [[Wat Tambor]] as Vader cut down [[Rute Gunnay]] before his eyes. This, however, did little more than delay their deaths by a few seconds and Vader killed both Haako and Tambor in quick succession, leaving only Gunray to fall moments after.<ref name="Episode III" />

==Personality and traits==
A mean and greedy individual, Rune Haako served as Viceroy Gunray's legal counsel when the two led the invasion of Naboo.<ref name="Rune's Card">{{ForceCollection|Rune Haako|star=2}}</ref> A male Neimoidian, Haako stood at 1.96 [[meter]]s tall<ref name="Databank" /> and had [[Color|red]]-gold eyes and green skin.<ref name="Episode I" />

==Equipment==
Rune Haako wore purple clothing and a crested fabric tiara during the Naboo Invasion.<ref name="Episode I" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:JeromeBlake.jpg|thumb|right|240px|Jerome Blake played Rune Haako]]
Rune Haako was played by [[Jerome Blake]] and voiced by [[James Taylor (voice actor)|James Taylor]] in [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''The Phantom Menace'']].<ref name="Episode I" /> In [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Attack of the Clones'']], he was played by [[Alan Ruscoe]] and voiced by [[Chris Truswell]] (despite the credits identifying him as [[Lott Dod]]),<ref name="Episode II" /> and played by [[Sandy Thompson]] in [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Revenge of the Sith'']].<ref name="Episode III" /> For ''The Phantom Menace'' Rune Haako's mask was sculpted by Gary Pollard.<ref name="100INTGP">{{YouTube|video=6fevC0IluiY|text=Gary Pollard - Creature Sculptor SW Ep 1 - FORCEMANIA (2023)|channel=Forcemania|name=Forcemania|date=2025-12-09}}</ref>

After filming for ''The Phantom Menace'' wrapped, Haako's mask was lost, resulting in the production crew giving Daultay Dofine's mask to Ruscoe instead, and for a time it was thought that this "new" Neimoidian would become a separate character named [[Gilramos Libkath]].<ref name="hcb">{{Blog|holocron|29|Mistaken Identities}}</ref> Within the new ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], Haako was confirmed to be the Neimoidian present in ''Attack of the Clones'' through the ''[[Star Wars: Geektionary: The Galaxy from A - Z]]'' reference book.<ref name="Geektionary">''[[Star Wars: Geektionary: The Galaxy from A - Z]]''</ref> While ''[[Star Wars: Card Trader]]'' misidentified the Neimoidian as Lott Dod in its [[2023]] Base Series<ref name="Lott 2023">{{SWCT|set=2023 Base|cardname=Lott Dod}}</ref> and [[2024]] Featured Creature series,<ref name="Lott 2024">{{SWCT|set=Featured Creature - 2024|cardname=Lott Dod - A Neimoidian}}</ref> the ''[[Star Wars: Unlimited]]'' card game affirmed that Haako was the Neimoidian in ''Attack of the Clones'' through his ''[[Twilight of the Republic]]'' card, which featured art by [[Sebastián Guidobono]].<ref name="Lott Twilight">{{SWU|set=Twilight of the Republic|cardname=Rune Haako|subtitle=Scheming Second|link=5333016146|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/f8Id5}}</ref>

A claim carried over from the diagram's [[Star Wars Legends|Legends]] printing in ''[[Inside the Worlds of Star Wars: Attack of the Clones]]'',<ref name="WorldsATOC">''[[Inside the Worlds of Star Wars: Attack of the Clones]]''</ref> [[2016]]'s ''[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|Star Wars: Complete Locations]]'' also claimed that Dodd was the Neimoidian present in ''Attack of the Clones'' via its diagram of the Petranaki arena.<ref name="CompleteLocations">''[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|Star Wars: Complete Locations]]''</ref> The text was corrected to be Haako in the book's [[2025]] update, ''[[Star Wars: Complete Locations, New Edition]]''.<ref name="CompleteLocationsNEw">''[[Star Wars: Complete Locations, New Edition]]''</ref> ''[[Star Wars: The Prequel Trilogy – A Graphic Novel]]'', a graphic novel adaptation of the [[prequel trilogy]], incorrectly depicts Haako as two separate characters, using Haako's appearance<ref name="PT Graphic Novel">''[[Star Wars: The Prequel Trilogy – A Graphic Novel]]''</ref> from ''The Phantom Menace''<ref name="Episode I" /> to represent him and his later<ref name="PT Graphic Novel" /> appearance from ''Attack of the Clones''<ref name="Episode II" /> as another character. In this adaptation, the character who<ref name="PT Graphic Novel" /> wears his ''Attack of the Clones'' robes<ref name="Episode II" /> walks behind Haako and Gunray in the hallway scene before the Geonosis summit. During the summit and arena battle, Haako stands with Gunray, while this other Neimoidian is present in the war room with Gunray. Additionally, this Neimoidian is given<ref name="PT Graphic Novel" /> Gunray's line<ref name="Episode II" /> about the Separatist Army's failing status in the battle, while Dooku is given<ref name="PT Graphic Novel" /> Haako's line<ref name="Episode II" /> about needing to send their starships into space.<ref name="PT Graphic Novel" />

